{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Noah","id":"360967589511561218","is_bot":0,"username":"king.crusader"},"author_id":"360967589511561218","channel_id":"733827680490881095","content":"Night hags were incredibly evil creatures that lived in the Lower Planes. They were known for their mercilessness and ability to walk in the dreams of others. They have a great affinity for nightmares and were known to cause sleep paralysis in people, particularly for a deeply held contempt for those accepted in specific castes of society. Night hags were about as tall as human women. They had ugly features and blue-violet skin covered with warts, blisters, and sores. Their eyes burned red with malevolence. Their hands ended in jet-black talons. The first hags were discovered by an explorer known as Christopher Columbus when he sailed to Arcania. There he shared his tales of fending off and defending his town from these evil creatures masquerading as women and was able to take care of them before his return to Spain.","created_at":"2020-08-05T04:10:59.421000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"740421573210538055","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
